              "tellMeMore": "scientists to work more than 30 meters up in the canopy while they collect species that live only at that level. Other researchers catalogue the organ- isms that live in coral reefs, and others attach radio collars to deer. Still others work in laboratories comparing the DNA of members of isolated popula- tions to see how or if these populations might be changing. Importance of Biodiversity Compare a parking lot covered with asphalt to your favorite place in nature, perhaps your backyard, a wooded area, or a local lake. Y ou might go to an area like this to relax or to think. Artists get inspiration from these areas for songs, paintings, photographs, and literature. Looking at one of Art Wolfe\u2019s photo- graphs in the Connection to Arton page 128 can help you appreciate the beauty biodiversity gives our world. Beyond beauty, why is biodiversity important?",
