              "tellMeMore": "(TEM) allows scientists to study the structures contained within a cell. New types of microscopes and new techniques are continually being de- signed. For example, the scanning tun- neling microscope (STM) uses the flow of electrons to create computer images of atoms on the surface of a molecule. New techniques using the light microscope have increased the information scientists can gain with this basic tool. Most of these new tech- niques seek to add contrast to struc- tures within the cells, such as adding dyes that stain some parts of a cell, but not others. T ry MiniLab 7.1to practice the basic technique of measuring objects under a microscope. Two Basic Cell Types With the development of better microscopes, scientists observed that all cells contain small, specialized structures called organelles. Many, but not all, organelles are surrounded by membranes.",
