              "tellMeMore": "Darwin on HMS Beagle It took Darwin years to develop his theory of evolution. He began in 1831 at age 22 when he took a job as a naturalist on the English ship HMS Beagle, which sailed around the world on a five-year scientific journey. As the ship\u2019s naturalist, Darwin studied and collected biological and fossil specimens at every port along the route. As you might imagine, these specimens were quite diverse. Studying the specimens made Darwin curious about possible relationships among species. His studies provided the foundation for his theory of evo- lution by natural selection. Darwin in the Gal\u00e1pagos The Gal\u00e1pagos (guh LAH puh gus) Islands are a group of small islands near the equator, about 1000 km off the west coast of South America. The observations that Darwin made and the specimens that he collected there were especially important to him.",
