              "tellMeMore": "Chapter 1 21 Places and Regions A place is a particular space with physical and human meaning. Every place on Earth has its own unique characteristics, determined by the surround- ing environment and the people who live there. One task of geographers is to understand and explain how places are similar to and different from one another. To interpret the earth\u2019s complexity, geographers often group places into regions, or areas united by specific factors. The defining factors of a region may be phys- ical, such as soil type, vegetation, river systems, and climate. A region may also have human factors that help define it. These may include language, religion, cultural traditions, forms of government, and trade networks. Geographers identify three types of regions: for- mal, functional, and perceptual.",
