              "tellMeMore": "82 Unit 1 Religion Another important part of culture is religion. Reli- gious beliefs vary significantly around the world, and struggles over religious differences are a source of conflict in many countries. In many cultures, however, religion enables people to find a sense of identity. It also influences aspects of daily life, from the practice of moral values to the celebration of hol- idays and festivals. Throughout history, religious symbols and stories have shaped cultural expres- sions such as painting, sculpture, architecture, music, and dance. Some of the major world religions are Hinduism, Buddhism, Judaism, Christianity, and Islam. The map above shows the areas of the world where these religions are practiced. Social Groups Every culture includes a social system in which the members of the society fall into various smaller groups.",
