              "tellMeMore": "Viewpoint Rivers are the lifeblood of arid regions. As rivers wind through parched landscapes, they supply precious water to millions of people. Anything that disrupts a river\u2019s flow can be a threat to life itself. So it is with Turkey\u2019s Atat\u00fcrk Dam on the Euphrates River. The Atat\u00fcrk restrains the Euphrates and diverts some of its water for irrigation. For the Turks, the dam is turning barren plains into lush croplands. Downstream, however, Syria and Iraq worry that the Atat\u00fcrk project will rob their countries of a vital lifeline. CASE STUDY on the Environment Atat\u00a8urk Dam TURKEY SYRIA IRAQ TigrisR.",
